-- Terms & Conditions / Privacy Policy content, editable from the admin panel.
-- Seeded with a genuine starting draft reflecting how King's Library actually works
-- today (manual purchase + grant, email-based sign-in, Supabase storage). This is a
-- draft, not legal advice — review with a professional before relying on it.
insert into public.settings (key, value) values
  ('terms_text', E'These Terms & Conditions govern your use of King''s Library (the "Service"), a digital platform for reading books and listening to podcasts. By creating an account or using the Service, you agree to these terms.\n\n<strong>Purchases and access.</strong> Currently, purchases are arranged directly with us — contact us using the email shown on this site to buy a book or podcast. Once payment is confirmed, we grant you access to the purchased content and email you a sign-in code. There is no automated payment processor at this time.\n\n<strong>Your account.</strong> Access is tied to the email address you provide. You are responsible for keeping your sign-in code confidential and not sharing your account access with others.\n\n<strong>Content usage.</strong> All books and podcasts remain the property of their respective authors and creators. Purchasing access grants you a personal, non-transferable license to read or listen to that content within King''s Library. You may not copy, redistribute, download, or share the content outside the platform.\n\n<strong>Refunds.</strong> Because access is granted individually after purchase, refund requests are handled on a case-by-case basis — contact us directly to discuss any issue with your purchase.\n\n<strong>Changes to these terms.</strong> We may update these terms from time to time. Continued use of the Service after changes take effect means you accept the updated terms.\n\n<strong>Contact.</strong> Questions about these terms can be sent to the contact email listed on this site.'),
  ('privacy_text', E'This Privacy Policy explains what information King''s Library collects and how it is used.\n\n<strong>Information we collect.</strong> We collect the email address you provide when you purchase access or sign in, along with basic usage information such as which books/podcasts you have been granted, your reading progress, and sign-in activity.\n\n<strong>How we use it.</strong> We use your email to create your account, send you sign-in codes, and notify you about new content or updates related to your purchases. We use reading/listening progress only to let you resume where you left off.\n\n<strong>Data storage.</strong> Your information is stored securely using Supabase, our backend provider, with access restricted to what is needed to operate the Service.\n\n<strong>Sharing.</strong> We do not sell or share your personal information with third parties, except as required to operate the Service (such as our email delivery provider, used only to send you account-related emails) or if required by law.\n\n<strong>Your choices.</strong> You can contact us at any time to ask what information we hold about you or to request that your account be removed.\n\n<strong>Changes to this policy.</strong> We may update this policy from time to time; continued use of the Service means you accept the current version.\n\n<strong>Contact.</strong> Questions about this policy can be sent to the contact email listed on this site.')
on conflict (key) do nothing;
